Terminals unused in grammar

   REPEAT
   UNTIL
   SWITCH
   CASE
   DEFAULT
   BREAK
   FUNCTION
   RETURN
   COMMA
   COLON


Grammar

    0 $accept: program $end

    1 program: statement

    2 statement: declaration_stmt
    3          | assignment_stmt
    4          | expression SEMICOLON
    5          | if_stmt
    6          | while_stmt
    7          | for_stmt

    8 declaration_stmt: type IDENTIFIER SEMICOLON
    9                 | CONST type IDENTIFIER ASSIGN expression SEMICOLON
   10                 | type IDENTIFIER ASSIGN expression SEMICOLON

   11 type: INT
   12     | FLOAT_TYPE
   13     | STRING_TYPE
   14     | CHAR_TYPE

   15 assignment_stmt: IDENTIFIER ASSIGN expression SEMICOLON

   16 assign: IDENTIFIER ASSIGN expression

   17 expression: expression PLUS T
   18           | expression MINUS T
   19           | T

   20 T: T MULTIPLY F
   21  | T DIVIDE F
   22  | T MODULO F
   23  | F

   24 F: LPAREN expression RPAREN
   25  | MINUS F
   26  | IDENTIFIER
   27  | FLOAT
   28  | NUMBER

   29 condition: expression EQUAL expression
   30          | expression NOT_EQUAL expression
   31          | expression LESS_THAN expression
   32          | expression GREATER_THAN expression
   33          | expression LESS_EQUAL expression
   34          | expression GREATER_EQUAL expression
   35          | expression AND expression
   36          | expression OR expression
   37          | NOT expression

   38 $@1: /* empty */

   39 if_stmt: IF LPAREN condition RPAREN LBRACE statement RBRACE $@1 IF LPAREN condition RPAREN LBRACE statement RBRACE ELSE LBRACE statement RBRACE

   40 while_stmt: WHILE LPAREN condition RPAREN LBRACE statement RBRACE

   41 for_stmt: FOR LPAREN declaration_stmt condition SEMICOLON assign RPAREN LBRACE statement RBRACE


